The '''2000 UEFA Super Cup''' was a [[Association football|football]] match played on 25 August 2000 between [[Real Madrid CF|Real Madrid]] of Spain and [[Galatasaray S.K. (football)|Galatasaray]] of Turkey. Real Madrid qualified by beating [[Valencia CF|Valencia]] in the [[2000 UEFA Champions League Final]], while Galatasaray had made it to the Super Cup after beating [[Arsenal F.C.|Arsenal]] in the [[2000 UEFA Cup Final]]. Galatasaray won the match 2–1, both goals scored by [[Mário Jardel]], the latter a [[golden goal]].<ref>[https://web.archive.org/web/20010503155837/http://www.uefa.com/SuperCup/news/index.asp?Page=1&News=6970 Report]</ref>

This was the first Super Cup contested by the winners of the UEFA Cup (now the [[UEFA Europa League]]). Until 1999, it was contested by the winners of the [[UEFA Champions League]] and the winners of the [[UEFA Cup Winners' Cup]], but the Cup Winners' Cup was discontinued after the 1998–99 season.

==Venue==
The [[Stade Louis II]] in [[Monaco]] has been the venue for the UEFA Super Cup since 1998.<ref name="pk-09"/> It was built in 1985, and is also the home of [[AS Monaco FC|AS Monaco]], who play in the French league system.

